class.description:
An action is two things at once. To [GoapPlanner] it is pure data: a set of [member preconditions] that must hold before it can run, and a set of [member effects] the planner assumes will hold once it has. To [GoapAgent] it is behavior, run through [method _enter], [method _tick] and [method _exit].
Extend this class to write an action:
[codeblock]
extends GoapAction

func _init():
    action_name = &"chop_wood"
    cost = 2.0
    preconditions = {&"has_axe": true}
    effects = {&"has_wood": true}

func _is_valid(context):
    return get_tree().get_first_node_in_group("trees") != null

func _tick(context, delta):
    if not context.agent.reached_target():
        return GoapAction.STATUS_RUNNING
    return GoapAction.STATUS_SUCCEEDED
[/codeblock]
An action without a [method _tick] override succeeds the moment it starts, which is useful for steps that only exist to move the world state forward.
Actions are resources with no per-agent state, so the same instance can be shared by every agent that knows how to perform it. Anything that varies between agents belongs in the [GoapContext].
